<section class="section" id="help" aria-labelledby="help-title">
  <p class="section__eyebrow reveal">How I can help</p>
  <h2 class="section__title reveal" id="help-title">A different kind of fit.</h2>
  <div class="section__lede reveal help-lede">
    <p>
      I specialise in working with people who have tried therapy before and left
      feeling stuck, unseen, or sure it “wasn’t for them.”
    </p>
    <p>
      Often it isn’t that therapy failed—it’s that the approach didn’t match you.
      This is a dedicated space to try again, without starting from scratch in the
      same old rigid way.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="help-stack">
    <div class="practice-layout reveal">
      <div class="approach-block">
        <h3>Who is this for?</h3>
        <p>
          If you’re carrying difficult past experiences and previous therapy didn’t
          quite land, you’re in the right place.
        </p>
        <p>
          When therapy doesn’t work, it is easy to assume that you were the issue—or
          to quietly decide that therapy simply isn’t worth another try. While we
          often play a key role in our own patterns and difficulties, struggling to
          benefit from a specific therapeutic approach doesn’t mean you are beyond
          help. Standard talk therapy often relies heavily on rigid structures or
          pure verbal analysis, which simply doesn’t suit how everyone processes
          distress.
        </p>
        <p>
          This space is for anyone looking to try a different way of working—one that
          adapts to how you actually think, feel, and experience the world, rather
          than expecting you to fit a fixed mold. You don’t need to know how to be a
          “good client” or have everything neatly articulated before we begin.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="approach-block">
        <h3>What we actually do</h3>
        <p>
          Integrative psychotherapy means I don’t stick to a single, rigid template.
          We draw on different modalities—integrating talk-based work with experiential
          tools—to find what actually resonates with you and your history, adjusting as we go.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a space to understand the “why” behind what you’re experiencing,
          untangle old narratives, separate past from future, and establish a gentler,
          more effective pace for change. The goal isn’t to erase hard feelings; it’s
          to help you drop the struggle with what’s keeping you stuck, stay grounded
          in what matters to you, and take steps toward living a life aligned with
          your values.
        </p>
        <p>
          We move at a pace that feels manageable. You will always know how and why we
          are working the way we are, and what you think remains firmly at the
          centre—not a theory, and not my agenda.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="scope-box reveal" tabindex="0" aria-label="Who I can and cannot work with">
      <div class="scope-box__columns">
        <div>
          <h3>Who I can work with</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Adolescents and young people</li>
            <li>Emotional-Based School Avoidance (EBSA) and school-related anxiety</li>
            <li>Neurodivergent individuals (e.g., ADHD, Autism without severe learning disabilities)</li>
            <li>Gender dysphoria and gender identity exploration</li>
            <li>Body dysmorphia and body image distress</li>
            <li>Individual relationship issues and attachment concerns</li>
            <li>Anxiety, Generalised Anxiety Disorder (GAD), and panic</li>
            <li>Stress and workplace or academic burnout</li>
            <li>Mild-to-moderate low mood and depression</li>
            <li>Identity, self-concept, and life transitions</li>
            <li>Clients seeking a hybrid of integrative psychotherapy and creative/musical processes</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Who I cannot work with</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Couples, marriages, or joint family therapy</li>
            <li>Acute psychiatric symptoms, active psychosis, or mania</li>
            <li>Active, high-risk suicidal ideation or acute crisis situations</li>
            <li>Progressive neurodegenerative conditions (e.g., Dementia, Alzheimer’s)</li>
            <li>Moderate-to-severe learning disabilities or severe non-verbal cognitive impairments</li>
            <li>Active, unmanaged substance dependence or addiction</li>
            <li>Severe, medically unstable eating disorders</li>
            <li>Court-mandated therapy, forensic cases, or medico-legal evaluations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Rates />
  </div>
</section>
